arm64: dts: h713: add the HY310 board dts

Until now the HY310 boots a DTB called sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1: the file
carries the HY310's hardware, but it is named after cstenger's HY200 bench
board, because that is the board the description was first written for. With
boards/ turning into one directory per board, every board needs a DTB name of
its own -- otherwise board.env cannot name the DTB, the FIT description lies
about what it carries, and a second board cannot be added at all without
renaming the first one's file (doku/121 section 3 "Kernel DTS").

So this adds a device tree that is nothing but a name:

  #include "sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts"
  / { model/compatible for the HY310 };

The SoC compatible string stays byte for byte what the included file uses,
"allwinner,sun50i-h713", so the same drivers bind; only the board compatible
becomes "magcubic,hy310". The resulting DTB is the HY200 one plus a different
model and board compatible -- no node, no property, no status changes, so an
HY310 that boots with the new DTB sees the hardware it saw before.

Everything HY310-specific that we patched into the hy200 dts stays where it
is. Moving it into this file (and leaving the bench board with a real bench
description) is a separate cleanup; doing it here would mean changing the
DTB the device boots and renaming it in one step.

Including a .dts from a .dts is the pattern mainline already uses two entries
above ours in the same Makefile: sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts includes
sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts and overrides model/compatible, and
sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-h.dts does the same on top of that. The /dts-v1/;
of the included file counts as this file's version tag, which is why there is
none here.

The vendor string "magcubic" is not in
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/vendor-prefixes.yaml (checked against the
pinned 6.18.38 tarball; neither is "cstenger", which patch 0024 already uses).
That matters the day this goes upstream, not for an out-of-tree series -- no
driver we ship matches on the board compatible.

diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-sp.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713-v2.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h713-hy310.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
diff -ruN a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy310.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+/*
+ * MagCubic HY310 projector (board silkscreen HY260_QZ713_V3.1).
+ *
+ * The hardware description lives in sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts; this
+ * board only carries its own name, so that the DTB the HY310 boots is not
+ * named after somebody else's board. Whatever is HY310-specific in the
+ * included file stays there for now -- splitting it out is a later cleanup,
+ * not part of this change (doku/121 section 3).
+ *
+ * Same pattern as sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dts, which includes
+ * sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts and overrides model/compatible.
+ */
+
+#include "sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts"
+
+/ {
+	model = "MagCubic HY310 (HY260_QZ713_V3.1)";
+	compatible = "magcubic,hy310", "allwinner,sun50i-h713";
+};
